    "cellCounter": 28,
    "cells": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "code": "# Tutorial del árbol genealógico con UnifyWeaver\n\nEste cuaderno de trabajo interactivo demuestra cómo usar UnifyWeaver para compilar predicados de Prolog a scripts de Bash.\n\n## Requisitos previos\n\n- SWI-Prolog instalado\n- Biblioteca UnifyWeaver disponible\n- Kernel de Jupyter para Prolog instalado (`pip install prolog-jupyter-kernel`)\n\n## Objetivos de aprendizaje\n\nAl final de este cuaderno de trabajo, podrás:\n1. Definir hechos y reglas de Prolog\n2. Usar UnifyWeaver para compilar predicados a Bash\n3. Probar los scripts de Bash generados\n4. Comprender la compilación de clausuras transitivas",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "code": "## Paso 1: Inicializar el entorno de UnifyWeaver\n\nEn primer lugar, necesitamos cargar los módulos de UnifyWeaver. Usaremos el archivo `init.pl` del directorio education.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "code": "% Cargar el archivo de inicialización\n['../init'].",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Cannot find file: ../init",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Cannot find file: ../init</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 4,
        "code": "## Paso 2: Definir relaciones familiares\n\nDefinamos algunas relaciones progenitor-hijo del árbol genealógico bíblico.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 5,
        "code": "% Definir los hechos de parent\n:- dynamic parent/2.\n\nparent(abraham, isaac).\nparent(abraham, ishmael).\nparent(isaac, jacob).\nparent(isaac, esau).\nparent(jacob, reuben).\nparent(jacob, simeon).\nparent(jacob, levi).\nparent(jacob, judah).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 6,
        "code": "## Paso 3: Probar consultas de parent\n\nAntes de compilar, verifiquemos que nuestros datos sean correctos con algunas consultas de Prolog.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 7,
        "code": "% Consulta: ¿Quiénes son los hijos de Abraham?\nparent(abraham, Child).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Child = isaac\nChild = ishmael",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Child = isaac\nChild = ishmael</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 8,
        "code": "% Consulta: ¿Quiénes son los hijos de Jacob?\nparent(jacob, Child).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Child = reuben\nChild = simeon\nChild = levi\nChild = judah",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Child = reuben\nChild = simeon\nChild = levi\nChild = judah</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 9,
        "code": "## Paso 4: Definir la relación ancestor\n\nAhora definamos la clausura transitiva: la relación `ancestor`.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 10,
        "code": "% Definir ancestor como la clausura transitiva de parent\n:- dynamic ancestor/2.\n\n% Caso base: el progenitor es un ancestro\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\n\n% Caso recursivo: si X es progenitor de Y e Y es ancestro de Z, entonces X es ancestro de Z\nancestor(X, Z) :- parent(X, Y), ancestor(Y, Z).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 11,
        "code": "## Paso 5: Probar consultas de ancestor\n\nVerifiquemos que nuestro predicado ancestor funcione correctamente.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 12,
        "code": "% Consulta: ¿Es Abraham un ancestro de Jacob?\n( ancestor(abraham, jacob) ->\n    writeln('Yes: Abraham is an ancestor of Jacob')\n;\n    writeln('No: Abraham is not an ancestor of Jacob')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Yes: Abraham is an ancestor of Jacob",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Yes: Abraham is an ancestor of Jacob</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 13,
        "code": "% Consulta: ¿Quiénes son todos los descendientes de Abraham?\nancestor(abraham, Descendant).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Descendant = isaac\nDescendant = ishmael\nDescendant = jacob\nDescendant = esau\nDescendant = reuben\nDescendant = simeon\nDescendant = levi\nDescendant = judah",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Descendant = isaac\nDescendant = ishmael\nDescendant = jacob\nDescendant = esau\nDescendant = reuben\nDescendant = simeon\nDescendant = levi\nDescendant = judah</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 14,
        "code": "## Paso 6: Compilar parent a Bash\n\nAhora la parte emocionante: ¡compilemos nuestros hechos `parent/2` a un script de Bash!",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 15,
        "code": "% Cargar el compilador de flujos\n\\+ \\+ (\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/stream_compiler)),\n\n    % Compilar los hechos parent a bash\n    stream_compiler:compile_facts(parent, 2, [], _BashCode),\n    writeln('Generated Bash code for parent/2:'),\n    writeln(_BashCode)\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "source_sink `unifyweaver(core/stream_compiler)' does not exist",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">source_sink `unifyweaver(core/stream_compiler)' does not exist</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 16,
        "code": "## Paso 7: Guardar el script de parent\n\nGuardemos el código Bash generado en un archivo.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 17,
        "code": "% Guardar en un archivo\n\\+ \\+ (\n    stream_compiler:compile_facts(parent, 2, [], _BashCode),\n    setup_call_cleanup(\n        open('../output/parent.sh', write, _Stream),\n        write(_Stream, _BashCode),\n        close(_Stream)),\n    writeln('Saved to ../output/parent.sh')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: stream_compiler:compile_facts/4",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: stream_compiler:compile_facts/4</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 18,
        "code": "## Paso 8: Compilar ancestor a Bash\n\nAhora compilemos el predicado `ancestor/2`, que utiliza recursión.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 19,
        "code": "% Cargar el compilador recursivo\n\\+ \\+ (\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)),\n\n    % Compilar ancestor a bash\n    compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [], _BashCode),\n    writeln('Generated Bash code for ancestor/2:'),\n    writeln(_BashCode)\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "source_sink `unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)' does not exist",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">source_sink `unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)' does not exist</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 20,
        "code": "## Paso 9: Guardar el script de ancestor\n\nGuarda el script de ancestor en un archivo.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 21,
        "code": "% Guardar en un archivo\n\\+ \\+ (\n    compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [], _BashCode),\n    setup_call_cleanup(\n        open('../output/ancestor.sh', write, _Stream),\n        write(_Stream, _BashCode),\n        close(_Stream)),\n    writeln('Saved to ../output/ancestor.sh')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: compile_recursive/3",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: compile_recursive/3</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 22,
        "code": "## Paso 10: Probar los scripts generados\n\n¡Ahora probemos nuestros scripts de Bash generados! Usaremos la magia `%%bash` para ejecutar comandos de bash.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 23,
        "code": "# Cargar el script parent\nsource ../output/parent.sh\n\n# Prueba: ¿Quiénes son los hijos de Abraham?\necho \"Hijos de Abraham:\"\nparent abraham",
        "type": "code",
